            <div class="qa">
              <div class="q" set:html={f.q}></div>
              <div class="a" set:html={f.a}></div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="cav">People also read</div>
        <h2>Keep going</h2>
        <div class="sec">
          <ul class="pillars">
            <li><span class="dot">&rarr;</span><div><b><a href="/playbooks/compound-interest/">How Compound Interest Rewards Starting Early</a></b> Turn the tax you keep into long-term growth, with nothing uploaded.</div></li>
            <li><span class="dot">&rarr;</span><div><b><a href="/playbooks/mortgage-calculator/">What Your Mortgage Payment Really Includes</a></b> The full monthly cost of a home, beyond principal and interest.</div></li>
            <li><span class="dot">&rarr;</span><div><b><a href="/playbooks/free-finance-tools/">Free Finance Tools, Nothing Uploaded</a></b> The privacy-first money toolkit, from bank statement conversion to invoices.</div></li>
            <li><span class="dot">&rarr;</span><div><b><a href="/knowledge-center/smb-ai-readiness/">SMB AI Readiness Score</a></b> A free assessment with an instant radar and quick wins.</div></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Sources</h2>
        <ul class="sources">
          <li>IRS, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-releases-tax-inflation-adjustments-for-tax-year-2026-including-amendments-from-the-one-big-beautiful-bill" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tax inflation adjustments for tax year 2026</a> (2026 brackets and standard deductions of $16,100 single, $32,200 married filing jointly, $24,150 head of household), Rev. Proc. 2025-32, 2025.</li>
          <li>IRS, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/self-employment-tax-social-security-and-medicare-taxes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Self-employment tax</a> (15.3% total, on 92.35% of net earnings, half deductible), current.</li>
          <li>Social Security Administration, <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/news/en/cola/factsheets/2026.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 fact sheet</a> ($184,500 Social Security wage base; employee FICA 7.65%), 2025.</li>
